    <Label Name="Title" Style="GalleryTitle" Text="Conic Through Five Points" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="36.25" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Any five points (no three on a line) determine exactly one conic section — an ellipse, a parabola or a hyperbola.\n\nThe red curve is that conic, drawn with a straightedge only: as M slides along the line, Pascal's theorem places the point A on the curve.\n\nDrag the five points and watch the ellipse become a hyperbola." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="84.25" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
